<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="no-js">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<title>Bridge Field Notes</title>
<meta name="description" content="The playful companion to the Bridge Milestones 1 to 3 Delivery Report. Same numbers, better lighting.">
<link rel="icon" href="assets/bridge-mark.svg">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
<script>document.documentElement.className="js";</script>
</head>
<body>

<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<!-- ═══ ambient smoke ═══ -->
<div class="smoke" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="smoke-layer smoke-a"></div>
  <div class="smoke-layer smoke-b"></div>
  <div class="smoke-layer smoke-c"></div>
</div>
<div class="grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<header class="topbar" data-topbar>
  <div class="topbar-in">
    <span class="topbar-brand">
      <img src="assets/bridge-mark.svg" alt="" width="34" height="21">
      <span class="topbar-word">BRIDGE</span>
    </span>
    <span class="topbar-meta">
      <span class="chip chip-21">21+</span>
      <span class="topbar-date">Companion read &middot; 3 Sept 2026</span>
    </span>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="main">

<!-- ══════════════════ 1 · INTRO ══════════════════ -->
<section class="intro" data-intro aria-labelledby="intro-h">
  <div class="intro-stage">

    <div class="wordmark-slot">
      <p class="wordmark" data-wordmark aria-label="Bridge">
        <span class="wm" data-wm><span class="wm-g">B</span><i class="wm-spark" aria-hidden="true"></i></span><span class="wm" data-wm><span class="wm-g">R</span><i class="wm-spark" aria-hidden="true"></i></span><span class="wm" data-wm><span class="wm-g">I</span><i class="wm-spark" aria-hidden="true"></i></span><span class="wm" data-wm><span class="wm-g">D</span><i class="wm-spark" aria-hidden="true"></i></span><span class="wm" data-wm><span class="wm-g">G</span><i class="wm-spark" aria-hidden="true"></i></span><span class="wm" data-wm><span class="wm-g">E</span><i class="wm-spark" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-object" data-rise="1">
      <img class="hero-mark" src="assets/bridge-mark.svg" alt="The Bridge arch mark" width="180" height="112">
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow" data-rise="2">The fun version</p>
    <h1 class="intro-h" id="intro-h" data-rise="3">Three milestones,<br>one very long<br><em>summer.</em></h1>
    <p class="intro-sub" data-rise="4">The serious thirteen&#8209;page report has every receipt in it. This is the same truth, with better lighting and a robot.</p>

    <p class="intro-meta" data-rise="5">
      <span>Momentum Digital, for Tori</span><span class="dot"></span><span>3 September 2026</span><span class="dot"></span><span>Evidence window 27 May to 3 Sept</span>
    </p>
    <p class="intro-fine" data-rise="6">Companion to the <em>Milestones 1 to 3 Delivery Report</em>. Every number on this page matches that one exactly, including the awkward ones.</p>

    <span class="scroll-cue" data-rise="6" aria-hidden="true"><span class="scroll-cue-rail"><span class="scroll-cue-dot"></span></span>scroll</span>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════ 2 · STATUS ══════════════════ -->
<section class="sec board" aria-labelledby="board-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker" data-lift>Where things actually stand</p>
    <h2 class="h2" id="board-h" data-lift>Four milestones. Two done,<br>one half&#8209;built, one untouched.</h2>
    <p class="lede" data-lift>No number on this page is rounded up and no status is nudged forward. If it says <em>in progress</em>, it is in progress.</p>

    <ol class="cards">
      <li class="card card-done" data-lift>
        <span class="card-stampwrap" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-stamptxt">DONE</span></span>
        <p class="card-no">Milestone 1</p>
        <h3 class="card-h">Discovery, Requirements&nbsp;and Architecture</h3>
        <p class="card-status"><span class="pip pip-done"></span>Delivered and paid</p>
        <p class="card-body">Your four concepts, the branding guide, the verification requirements and the compliance strategy became the actual product spec. That spec set the roles, the MVP boundary, the architecture, and the rules now baked into every screen.</p>
        <p class="card-note">Warmly received. &ldquo;The specs are awesome, the research is top tier.&rdquo; It was never captured as a dated acceptance, though. Worth closing retrospectively.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card card-done" data-lift>
        <span class="card-stampwrap" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-stamptxt">LIVE</span></span>
        <p class="card-no">Milestone 2</p>
        <h3 class="card-h">UX, Product Flow and the Data Model</h3>
        <p class="card-status"><span class="pip pip-done"></span>Delivered &middot; live for review</p>
        <p class="card-body">Home, Community News, Create, My Profile and Explore are all built, deployed and QA&rsquo;d on desktop and mobile, with the schema and permission rules behind them.</p>
        <p class="card-note card-note-warm"><strong>Not signed off.</strong> The acceptance record&rsquo;s decision column is still empty for all five routes. That is the one thing this whole page is quietly asking for.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card card-wip" data-lift>
        <span class="card-stampwrap" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-stamptxt">WIP</span></span>
        <p class="card-no">Milestone 3</p>
        <h3 class="card-h">Accounts, Authentication and&nbsp;Verification</h3>
        <p class="card-status"><span class="pip pip-wip"></span>Functionally complete, awaiting merge</p>
        <p class="card-body">The join sequence, sign&#8209;in, role&#8209;aware routing and the admin verification queue are built and passing every automated check. Greencubes delivered overnight, and their backend now has real server&#8209;side security in it. We checked that ourselves this morning rather than taking the summary on trust.</p>
        <p class="card-note">Not live yet, and the difference matters. The frontend pull request is open, not merged, so three Milestone&nbsp;3 routes still return 404 in production. Greencubes have asked for that commit on the dev preview first so they can verify it, which is the right order.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card card-none" data-lift>
        <span class="card-stampwrap" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-stamptxt">0%</span></span>
        <p class="card-no">Milestone 4</p>
        <h3 class="card-h">Directory MVP</h3>
        <p class="card-status"><span class="pip pip-none"></span>Not started</p>
        <p class="card-body">No work has begun. None. Zero commits, no branch, no sneaky head start.</p>
        <p class="card-note">Explore and the profile screens are Milestone&nbsp;2 UX running on sample data. Lovely, but not a directory. Production data, connected search, the claim&#8209;and&#8209;correction workflow and contact routing all live here.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════ 3 · PINNED CENTREPIECE ══════════════════ -->
<section class="pin" data-pin aria-labelledby="pin-h">
  <div class="pin-sticky">
    <div class="pin-inner">

      <div class="pin-head">
        <p class="kicker kicker-c">The build, turned over</p>
        <h2 class="h2 h2-c" id="pin-h">Everything we made,<br>from every angle.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="rig" data-rig>
        <div class="rig-box" data-box>
          <div class="face face-front">
            <img src="assets/bridge-mark.svg" alt="The Bridge arch mark" width="180" height="112">
          </div>
          <div class="face face-back">
            <p class="face-word">BRIDGE</p>
            <p class="face-tag">Connect. Grow.<br>Fight Together.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="face face-right"></div>
          <div class="face face-left"></div>
          <div class="face face-top"></div>
          <div class="face face-bottom"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="rig-shadow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="rail" aria-hidden="true"><span class="rail-line"></span></div>

      <ul class="callouts" data-callouts>
        <li class="callout" data-at="0"><b>12 member roles</b><span>a twelve&#8209;role grid, live</span></li>
        <li class="callout" data-at="0"><b>50 states + D.C.</b><span>enumerated on Explore</span></li>
        <li class="callout" data-at="1"><b>13 routes</b><span>returning 200 in production</span></li>
        <li class="callout" data-at="1"><b>3 legacy redirects</b><span>301, each to the right place</span></li>
        <li class="callout" data-at="2"><b>45 tests passing</b><span>zero failing</span></li>
        <li class="callout" data-at="2"><b>7 contrast fixes</b><span>measured, not asserted</span></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="caps" data-caps>
        <p class="cap" data-cap="0">Milestone 1, the foundation</p>
        <p class="cap" data-cap="1">Milestone 2, the product system</p>
        <p class="cap" data-cap="2">Milestone 3, the front door</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="takeover" data-takeover>
        <img src="assets/shots/d-home.webp" alt="The Bridge Home route captured live from production on 3 September 2026" width="1240" height="775">
        <figcaption>Home &middot; captured live from production, 3 September 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════ 4 · LOOKS FINISHED ══════════════════ -->
<section class="sec claim-a" aria-labelledby="mock-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="h2 h2-xl" id="mock-h" data-lift>Looks finished.<br><em>Isn&rsquo;t finished.</em></h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div data-lift>
        <p class="lede">Every screen on the review build runs against a typed mock adapter, and every screen <em>says so, on the page</em>. That was on purpose. It let you judge the product before a single dollar of backend cost was committed.</p>
        <p class="body">Turning mock mode off is one environment variable. As of this morning the backend origin is known and answering, so what is left is the merge and a dev preview deploy to verify against.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Explore says its sample records are limited and favourites stay on your device.</li>
          <li>Create says drafts and library actions stay local until the production API is connected.</li>
          <li>My Profile says the email reminder integration is pending.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="body body-em">Nothing on the review build implies a capability that isn&rsquo;t there. That was the whole discipline.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-hold" data-lift>
        <svg class="dgm" viewBox="0 0 300 210" role="img" aria-label="Diagram: the front end connects to a typed mock adapter today, and to the real backend once one environment variable flips.">
          <rect x="8" y="16" width="112" height="52" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="#C9ACFF" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          <text x="64" y="40" class="dgm-t" text-anchor="middle">Front end</text>
          <text x="64" y="56" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">13 routes, live</text>

          <rect x="180" y="16" width="112" height="52" rx="10" fill="#1E1330" stroke="#7BC98A" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          <text x="236" y="40" class="dgm-t" text-anchor="middle">Mock adapter</text>
          <text x="236" y="56" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">typed &middot; labelled</text>

          <path d="M122 42h54" stroke="#7BC98A" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/>
          <path d="M170 37l7 5-7 5z" fill="#7BC98A"/>
          <text x="149" y="32" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">today</text>

          <rect x="180" y="138" width="112" height="52" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="#5C4A78" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/>
          <text x="236" y="162" class="dgm-t dgm-dim" text-anchor="middle">Real backend</text>
          <text x="236" y="178" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">awaiting merge</text>

          <path d="M64 68v96h108" stroke="#5C4A78" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/>
          <path d="M166 159l7 5-7 5z" fill="#5C4A78"/>
          <rect x="70" y="100" width="104" height="26" rx="13" fill="#0A0610" stroke="#F0B45E" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text x="122" y="117" class="dgm-s dgm-warn" text-anchor="middle">1 env variable</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════ 5 · RECEIPTS ══════════════════ -->
<section class="sec receipts" aria-labelledby="num-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker" data-lift>The receipts wall</p>
    <h2 class="h2" id="num-h" data-lift>Twelve numbers, each one<br>checked by hand this morning.</h2>
    <p class="lede" data-lift>Nothing carried forward from an older report. Every figure below was probed, counted or re&#8209;run on 3 September.</p>

    <ul class="stats">
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>13</b><span>routes returning 200 in production</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>45</b><span>automated tests passing, zero failing</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>12</b><span>member roles defined and built</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>36</b><span>static pages in the production build</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>7</b><span>contrast failures found and fixed</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>3</b><span>themes checked for AA compliance</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>77</b><span>commits on the development branch</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>15<i>&thinsp;/&thinsp;</i>9</b><span>pull requests opened, then merged</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>2</b><span>deploy environments running</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>3</b><span>legacy paths redirecting correctly</span></li>
      <li class="stat" data-lift><b>50<i>+</i></b><span>states plus D.C. on Explore</span></li>
      <li class="stat stat-warm" data-lift><b>0</b><span>client acceptances recorded with a date</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="counted" data-lift>
      <img class="counted-bot" src="assets/mascot-sit.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="200" height="200">
      <p class="fineprint">That last one isn&rsquo;t a joke and it isn&rsquo;t a complaint. It&rsquo;s just the honest count, and it&rsquo;s the easiest number on this wall to change.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════ 6 · CAROUSEL ══════════════════ -->
<section class="sec routes" aria-labelledby="routes-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="routes-head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker" data-lift>The five routes waiting on you</p>
        <h2 class="h2" id="routes-h" data-lift>Milestone 2, in five<br>polaroids.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="carousel-ctl" data-lift>
        <button class="cbtn" type="button" data-prev aria-label="Previous route">&lsaquo;</button>
        <span class="cbtn-count" data-count aria-live="polite">1 / 5</span>
        <button class="cbtn" type="button" data-next aria-label="Next route">&rsaquo;</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="track" data-track tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="The five Milestone 2 review routes">
    <article class="poly" data-slide>
      <img class="poly-tape" src="assets/ephemera.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="poly-shot" src="assets/shots/d-home.webp" alt="The Home route" width="1240" height="775">
      <div class="poly-cap">
        <h3>Home</h3>
        <p>A compact product introduction with legal cannabis positioning, one primary join action, and one&#8209;click access to the four main spaces.</p>
        <p class="poly-tag">Pending Tori</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="poly" data-slide>
      <img class="poly-tape" src="assets/ephemera.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="poly-shot" src="assets/shots/d-community.webp" alt="The Community News route" width="1240" height="775">
      <div class="poly-cap">
        <h3>Community News</h3>
        <p>The same items as either a visual News Grid or a classic chronological feed, with category and state controls, favourites, and an explicit selected state. Non&#8209;algorithmic by design for the MVP.</p>
        <p class="poly-tag poly-tag-warm">Pending, default view undecided</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="poly" data-slide>
      <img class="poly-tape" src="assets/ephemera.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="poly-shot" src="assets/shots/d-create.webp" alt="The Create route" width="1240" height="775">
      <div class="poly-cap">
        <h3>Create</h3>
        <p>Promotion and message composition: content type, upload validation, multi&#8209;audience selection, live preview, and a guardrail that strips protected detail out of public targeting automatically.</p>
        <p class="poly-tag">Pending Tori</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="poly" data-slide>
      <img class="poly-tape" src="assets/ephemera.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="poly-shot" src="assets/shots/d-my-profile.webp" alt="The My Profile route" width="1240" height="775">
      <div class="poly-cap">
        <h3>My Profile</h3>
        <p>Two projections of one record, Public and B2B verified, with protected sales and accounting contacts, no public EIN, and a required first&#8209;login and monthly contact confirmation.</p>
        <p class="poly-tag">Pending Tori</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="poly" data-slide>
      <img class="poly-tape" src="assets/ephemera.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="poly-shot" src="assets/shots/d-explore.webp" alt="The Explore route" width="1240" height="775">
      <div class="poly-cap">
        <h3>Explore</h3>
        <p>Nationwide discovery across all fifty states and D.C., with category and role filters, a visible result count, persisted favourites, and a permissioned introduction request.</p>
        <p class="poly-tag">Pending Tori</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="fineprint fineprint-wide" data-lift>All five were sent for sign&#8209;off on 17 August. A review was promised on the 18th, again on the 23rd, and again on 1 September. On 21 August we wrote to the team, in writing, that these routes are <em>not officially approved yet</em>. That is still true, and this page holds to it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════ 7 · CLAIM BLOCKS ══════════════════ -->
<section class="sec claims" aria-labelledby="claims-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="sr-only" id="claims-h">Three things we got right that nobody will ever notice</h2>
    <p class="kicker" data-lift>Three things nobody will ever notice</p>
    <h2 class="h2" data-lift>The unglamorous work,<br>briefly glamorised.</h2>

    <div class="claim" data-lift>
      <div class="claim-txt">
        <h3 class="claim-h">Client routing is presentation.<br><em>Never permission.</em></h3>
        <p class="body">Sign&#8209;in sends members to their profile and administrators to the admin workspace. The return&#8209;path parameter accepts only same&#8209;origin paths. Absolute URLs and protocol&#8209;relative hosts get rejected. And every routing rule carries an explicit note that the API must still enforce it anyway.</p>
        <p class="body">No token in browser storage. The session is read from the API on each load, as a cookie session requires. There is a test that fails if any client file so much as touches web storage.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="dgm dgm-wide" viewBox="0 0 320 150" role="img" aria-label="Diagram: the browser routes for presentation only; the API is the gate that actually enforces permission.">
        <rect x="6" y="40" width="86" height="64" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="#C9ACFF" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="49" y="66" class="dgm-t" text-anchor="middle">Browser</text>
        <text x="49" y="82" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">routes you</text>
        <path d="M94 72h44" stroke="#5C4A78" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M132 67l7 5-7 5z" fill="#5C4A78"/>
        <rect x="140" y="30" width="24" height="84" rx="6" fill="#F0B45E" opacity=".16"/>
        <path d="M152 30v84" stroke="#F0B45E" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="152" y="22" class="dgm-s dgm-warn" text-anchor="middle">the gate</text>
        <path d="M166 72h34" stroke="#5C4A78" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M194 67l7 5-7 5z" fill="#5C4A78"/>
        <rect x="206" y="40" width="108" height="64" rx="10" fill="#1E1330" stroke="#7BC98A" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="260" y="62" class="dgm-t" text-anchor="middle">API</text>
        <text x="260" y="78" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">decides</text>
        <text x="260" y="92" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">every time</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="claim claim-flip" data-lift>
      <div class="claim-txt">
        <h3 class="claim-h">Contrast measured,<br><em>not asserted.</em></h3>
        <p class="body">An automated check implements the published contrast formulas, reads the colour tokens straight out of the stylesheet so the measured values can never drift from what actually ships, and asserts the AA threshold for every text&#8209;on&#8209;background pair, in all three themes.</p>
        <p class="body">Five failures in the admin panel, the worst at 2.88:1 against a 4.5:1 requirement. Two more hiding in the existing theme tokens that nobody knew about, including form error text at 2.22:1, which is to say <em>effectively invisible</em>. It now measures 6.02:1.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="dgm dgm-wide" viewBox="0 0 320 150" role="img" aria-label="Chart: form error text moved from 2.22 to 1 contrast, below the 4.5 to 1 AA threshold, up to 6.02 to 1, above it.">
        <line x1="40" y1="18" x2="40" y2="128" stroke="#3A2A50" stroke-width="1"/>
        <line x1="40" y1="128" x2="312" y2="128" stroke="#3A2A50" stroke-width="1"/>
        <line x1="40" y1="70" x2="312" y2="70" stroke="#F0B45E" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/>
        <text x="44" y="63" class="dgm-s dgm-warn">AA threshold 4.5:1</text>
        <rect x="86" y="99" width="64" height="29" rx="4" fill="#FF8A7A" opacity=".85"/>
        <text x="118" y="93" class="dgm-t" text-anchor="middle">2.22:1</text>
        <text x="118" y="143" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">before</text>
        <rect x="204" y="49" width="64" height="79" rx="4" fill="#7BC98A" opacity=".9"/>
        <text x="236" y="43" class="dgm-t" text-anchor="middle">6.02:1</text>
        <text x="236" y="143" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">after</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="claim" data-lift>
      <div class="claim-txt">
        <h3 class="claim-h">One HTTP client.<br><em>One contract.</em></h3>
        <p class="body">Registration, sign&#8209;in and sign&#8209;out went into the same typed client every other call already used, so they inherit one base URL, one status mapping and one error type. A second, parallel client that had quietly bypassed all of that got folded back in.</p>
        <p class="body">Error text is filtered too: only a curated, human message reaches the screen. A stack trace or a raw backend string physically cannot get in front of a member.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="dgm dgm-wide" viewBox="0 0 356 150" role="img" aria-label="Diagram: two HTTP clients folded into one, mapping to four status codes.">
        <rect x="6" y="26" width="78" height="34" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#5C4A78" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/>
        <text x="45" y="47" class="dgm-s dgm-dim" text-anchor="middle">rogue client</text>
        <rect x="6" y="90" width="78" height="34" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#C9ACFF" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="45" y="111" class="dgm-s" text-anchor="middle">typed client</text>
        <path d="M86 43c26 0 22 32 40 32" stroke="#5C4A78" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/>
        <path d="M86 107c26 0 22-32 40-32" stroke="#C9ACFF" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/>
        <rect x="128" y="58" width="66" height="34" rx="8" fill="#1E1330" stroke="#7BC98A" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="161" y="79" class="dgm-t" text-anchor="middle">one client</text>
        <path d="M196 75h22" stroke="#5C4A78" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M212 70l7 5-7 5z" fill="#5C4A78"/>
        <text x="226" y="38" class="dgm-s">401 &nbsp;unauthenticated</text>
        <text x="226" y="62" class="dgm-s">403 &nbsp;forbidden</text>
        <text x="226" y="86" class="dgm-s">400 / 422 &nbsp;validation</text>
        <text x="226" y="110" class="dgm-s">409 &nbsp;conflict</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════ 7B · VERIFIED OVERNIGHT ══════════════════ -->
<section class="sec verified" aria-labelledby="verified-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker" data-lift>Rewritten this morning, after Greencubes delivered</p>
    <h2 class="h2" id="verified-h" data-lift>The cookie decision landed.<br><em>Both rules held.</em></h2>
    <p class="lede" data-lift>Greencubes shipped overnight. We went and checked it ourselves rather than taking the summary on trust, and it holds up. This is the good news section, and it is genuinely theirs.</p>

    <ul class="ticks" data-lift>
      <li>The one missing response header is now present, so credentialed cookie sessions work and the test that was failing because of it is no longer blocked.</li>
      <li>The session endpoint and the identity endpoint both reject an unauthenticated caller with a 401. Server&#8209;side enforcement is real, not a client convention.</li>
      <li>Browser storage for tokens is gone from the frontend. The file that held it no longer exists.</li>
      <li>The duplicate HTTP client is gone too, so authentication finally routes through the one typed client with the one error contract.</li>
      <li>The reference join sequence was adopted rather than rebuilt, and Step 2 now lives at its own route.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="body body-em" data-lift>Those last two are the exact rules we set out in the section above, checked against somebody else&rsquo;s code. They held.</p>
    <p class="body" data-lift>Greencubes additionally report that sign&#8209;in issues secure cookies, that sign&#8209;out clears them and revokes the refresh session, that the session endpoint returns 401 afterwards, and that role enforcement stays server&#8209;side. Those are their words rather than our measurement, and this page marks the difference deliberately.</p>

    <p class="fineprint fineprint-wide" data-lift>One item is still open and it is small: a four&#8209;line pointer in the project instructions file still names the old repository instead of the current frontend one. Past that, the only reason none of this is live is that the pull request is open and unmerged.</p>
  </div>
</section>

