<!-- ══════════════════ 10 · JOIN LADDER ══════════════════ -->
<section class="sec ladder" aria-labelledby="ladder-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker" data-lift>Four steps, two of them waiting on a human</p>
    <h2 class="h2" id="ladder-h" data-lift>The join sequence,<br>honestly labelled.</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step step-live" data-lift>
        <p class="step-n">Step 1 of 4</p><p class="step-r">/join</p>
        <h3 class="step-h">Pick your role</h3>
        <p class="body">A twelve&#8209;role grid with per&#8209;role next&#8209;step titles and requirements, the founding&#8209;member callout, and a boundary note explaining what Steps 2 to 4 will need.</p>
        <p class="step-s"><span class="pip pip-done"></span>Live in production</p>
        <figure class="step-proof"><img src="assets/shots/d-join.webp" alt="Join Step 1, the twelve-role grid, captured live from production" width="1240" height="775"><figcaption>captured live, 3 Sept</figcaption></figure>
      </li>
      <li class="step step-built" data-lift>
        <p class="step-n">Step 2 of 4</p><p class="step-r">/join/account</p>
        <h3 class="step-h">Create the account</h3>
        <p class="body">Display name, email, password and confirmation, showing the role you chose in Step 1 with a link back to change it. Full inline validation and error states.</p>
        <p class="step-s"><span class="pip pip-wip"></span>Built &middot; pending merge</p>
      </li>
      <li class="step step-wait" data-lift>
        <p class="step-n">Step 3 of 4</p><p class="step-r">no route yet</p>
        <h3 class="step-h">Organization details</h3>
        <p class="body">Legal name, public name, EIN, licence, location and contact owner. Needs organization&#8209;scoped draft persistence, which is backend&#8209;owned.</p>
        <p class="step-s"><span class="pip pip-none"></span>Awaiting backend + approval</p>
      </li>
      <li class="step step-wait" data-lift>
        <p class="step-n">Step 4 of 4</p><p class="step-r">no route yet</p>
        <h3 class="step-h">Verification evidence</h3>
        <p class="body">Server&#8209;created upload intents, document scanning, a redacted review summary and a verification case.</p>
        <p class="step-s"><span class="pip pip-none"></span>Awaiting backend + approval</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="fineprint fineprint-wide" data-lift>Steps 3 and 4 aren&rsquo;t missing routes and they aren&rsquo;t a hosting problem. Real member identity now exists, which was the largest of the four backend pieces. What is still outstanding is organization&#8209;scoped drafts, protected evidence storage and a review case, plus a product answer on what evidence each of the twelve roles must supply and what the public &ldquo;Verified&rdquo; badge actually promises.</p>
  </div>
</section>

